        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string encoding="cdata"><![CDATA[

Recursively read a document and all nested sub-objects as a tree in one call.\n
\n
    Walks the document hierarchy (e.g. Sale Order -> Lines -> sub-lines) by following\n
    listbox children at each level. Uses compact field format (values only, no metadata).\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need the complete document tree (parent + all children + grandchildren).\n
    - Dealing with hierarchical documents: Sale Orders, Projects, Support Requests with events.\n
    - You want a compact overview of an entire document structure.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need full field details (editability, type, items) - use erp5_read for one document.\n
    - You need MatrixBox data - read_deep uses the default view which may not show matrices.\n
      Use erp5_read with view=\'quantity_view\' or \'price_view\' for matrix fields.\n
    - You only need the parent document without children - use erp5_read (faster, more detail).\n
    - You need to search for documents - use erp5_search first, then read_deep on results.\n
\n
    OUTPUT FORMAT: Returns a tree where each node has \'relative_url\', \'title\', \'portal_type\',\n
    \'fields\' (compact key:value pairs), and \'children\' (recursive). Common fields shared by\n
    all siblings are deduplicated into \'children_common_fields\' on the parent.\n
    

]]></string> </value>
